---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const situations: [string, boolean][] = [
  ['Automating your own house', true],
  ['A hobby project you are building for fun', true],
  ['A class project or a student lab', true],
  ['A local nonprofit running it in their own space', true],
  ['Running it inside a company, internal only, no customers touching it', false],
  ['Deploying it as part of a product or service you sell', false],
  ['A landlord automating a rental property they operate as a business', false],
  ['A contractor installing and managing it for paying clients', false],
];
---

<Base
  title="HotLoop license: Gateway and Flow explained"
  description="HotLoop Gateway is free for individuals, with business use through Embernet. HotLoop Flow is Apache-2.0, free for everyone, businesses included."
  ogAlt="HotLoop licensing, in plain language."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap stack">
      <span class="label">License</span>
      <h1>Which license applies to you?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Two products, licensed separately on purpose. We would rather tell you which one applies than have you
        find out later.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap body stack">
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data stack">
        <thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Who</th><th>Cost</th><th>How to get it</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>HotLoop Gateway</td>
            <td data-label="Who">Individual, home, hobbyist, nonprofit, or education</td>
            <td data-label="Cost"><span class="chip ok">Free</span></td>
            <td data-label="How to get it">Self-host directly, no agreement needed</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>HotLoop Gateway</td>
            <td data-label="Who">Any business or for-profit use, internal or customer-facing</td>
            <td data-label="Cost"><span class="chip info">Through Embernet</span></td>
            <td data-label="How to get it">Exclusively through <a href="https://embernet.ai">Embernet</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>HotLoop Flow</td>
            <td data-label="Who">Anyone, including businesses and commercial use</td>
            <td data-label="Cost"><span class="chip ok">Free</span></td>
            <td data-label="How to get it">Self-host directly under Apache-2.0, no agreement needed</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>HotLoop Flow is Apache-2.0</h2>
    <p>
      Flow is licensed under the <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0">Apache License, Version 2.0</a>,
      which is an OSI-approved open source license with no business-use restriction. A business can run it, modify it,
      and ship it commercially without asking anyone, and it does not need Embernet or anybody else's permission.
    </p>

    <h2>HotLoop Gateway is source-available</h2>
    <p>
      The Gateway is under the HotLoop Community License. It is source-available and it is <strong>not</strong> an
      OSI-approved open source license, because it restricts business use. Individuals get it free, and any business
      that wants it goes through our partner <a href="https://embernet.ai">Embernet</a>, which provides the support,
      the SLAs, and the warranty. That is not us crippling the free version to squeeze you later. It is a real
      partnership.
    </p>
    <p>A few concrete situations for the Gateway, because “business use” gets fuzzy fast once people start talking themselves into it.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data">
        <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Cost</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {situations.map(([s, free]) => (
            <tr><td>{s}</td><td class="cost">{free ? <span class="chip ok">Free</span> : <span class="chip info">Through Embernet</span>}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">
      Genuinely unsure which side of the Gateway line you are on? Ask before you build a whole setup on a bad
      assumption. Email <a href="mailto:support@hotloop.io">support@hotloop.io</a>, or go straight to Embernet if it
      looks like a business case.
    </p>

    <h2>One note on history</h2>
    <p>
      So nobody finds this by surprise. Container images for earlier versions of what is now HotLoop Gateway, versions
      4.0.0 through 4.3.1, were published publicly under Apache-2.0, along with the Helm chart packages released beside
      them. They remain available, and they remain under Apache-2.0. The HotLoop Community License applies to the
      Gateway from its first release under the HotLoop name onward. HotLoop Flow, first published as Emberwire, has been
      Apache-2.0 the whole time and is not changing.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      The plain-language version above is a summary. The legal text wins every argument, including this one. The
      Gateway's is in the <a href="https://github.com/HotLoop-io/HotLoop-io/blob/main/LICENSE.md">HotLoop-io/HotLoop-io</a>
      repository and mirrored on the <a href="https://docs.hotloop.io/licensing.html">docs site</a>, including the note
      it carries about legal review.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero { padding-block: clamp(var(--hl-s7), 7vw, var(--hl-s9)) var(--hl-s6); }
  .body { max-width: 860px; padding-bottom: var(--hl-s8); }
  .body h2 { font-size: var(--hl-fs-xl); margin-top: var(--hl-s7); }
  td.cost { width: 1%; white-space: nowrap; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { td.cost { white-space: normal; } }
</style>
